      "artist": "Ghulam Ali Khan",
      "credit": "[1]",
      "source": "Ghulam Ali Khan 007",
      "description": "The Dewan Am - and the Buildings occupied by the Heir Apparent in the Red Fort. \nA series of 31 paintings by Ghulam Ali Khan (fl. 1817-55), consisting of views of monuments in and around Delhi, and including four portraits of the last Mughal Emperor Bahadur Shah II (reg. 1837-58) and his sons. Watercolour and gold on paper, black margin rules, three title pages, three sheets of portraits, all with identifying inscriptions in English and in Persian in nasta'liq script in black ink, the portraits with further inscriptions in nasta'liq script with the date November 1852 (Christian date written in Arabic), in later mounts, loose in contemporary green leather-covered despatch box, the lid embossed in gold DELHEE 1854. \n\nSize paintings 290 x 215 mm. and slightly smaller; mounts 318 x 394 mm.; box 435 x 365 x 110 mm.",
      "dateCreated": "between circa 1852 and circa 1854<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P,+1852-00-00T00:00:00Z/8,P1319,+1852-00-00T00:00:00Z/9,P1326,+1854-00-00T00:00:00Z/9,P1480,Q5727902</div>",
